{
  "sn14.10:0.1": "Linked Discourses 14.10 ",
  "sn14.10:0.2": "1. Diversity ",
  "sn14.10:0.3": "No Diversity of Gains ",
  "sn14.10:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn14.10:1.2": "“Mendicants, diversity of elements gives rise to diversity of perceptions. ",
  "sn14.10:1.3": "Diversity of perceptions gives rise to diversity of thoughts. … ",
  "sn14.10:1.4": "contacts … ",
  "sn14.10:1.5": "feelings … ",
  "sn14.10:1.6": "desires … ",
  "sn14.10:1.7": "passions … ",
  "sn14.10:1.8": "Diversity of searches gives rise to diversity of gains. ",
  "sn14.10:1.9": "Diversity of gains doesn’t give rise to diversity of searches. ",
  "sn14.10:1.10": "Diversity of searches doesn’t give rise to diversity of passions. … ",
  "sn14.10:1.11": "desires … ",
  "sn14.10:1.12": "feelings … ",
  "sn14.10:1.13": "contacts … ",
  "sn14.10:1.14": "thoughts … ",
  "sn14.10:1.15": "Diversity of perceptions doesn’t give rise to diversity of elements. ",
  "sn14.10:1.16": "And what is the diversity of elements? ",
  "sn14.10:1.17": "The sight element, the sound element, the smell element, the taste element, the touch element, and the idea element. ",
  "sn14.10:1.18": "This is called the diversity of elements. ",
  "sn14.10:2.1": "And how does diversity of elements give rise to diversity of perceptions, ",
  "sn14.10:2.2": "and diversity of perceptions give rise to diversity of thoughts? ",
  "sn14.10:2.3": "contacts … ",
  "sn14.10:2.4": "feelings … ",
  "sn14.10:2.5": "desires … ",
  "sn14.10:2.6": "pas